<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1910">1910</a>–<a href="/years/1952">1952</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi was Nawab of Pataudi from 1917 and a cricketer who played Test cricket for both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He scored a century on his Test debut during the Bodyline series in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> in 1932–33, and in 1946 captained India on its tour of England. He died while playing polo in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1952. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansoor-ali-khan-pataudi">Mansoor Ali Khan Pataudi</a> also captained India.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iftikhar-ali-khan-pataudi.jpg" alt="Iftikhar Ali Khan Pataudi" width="320" height="474" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iftikhar_Ali_Khan_Pataudi_1931cr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
